 ## D9 — Require a fresh full-packet replay before packaging
 
 The return patch was applied to a complete new extraction of the issued packet rather than tested only in the edited workspace. The replay preserved the final generator hash and identified exactly six task-local source changes. The reconstructed checkout then passed all 359 selected-task tests. This guards against undeclared local state, missing patch members, and evidence that cannot survive handoff.
+
+## Current bounded peer finding: color-frequency shortcut
+
+On unchanged source `9700fc52f3edcf201ba01d2339fee11732ba09efbfd8d2875cd5bd624114a827`,
+seed 29 / easy / default sample indices 0,1,2 admit a plausible alternative:
+choose the least globally frequent nonzero covering color, breaking ties by
+numeric color. It matches all three actual Racket demonstration outputs but
+differs at one cell on default sample 3. All four inputs are lawful 8×8 draws.
+The current adjacent-priority lesson checker returns no findings for this case;
+that checker never promised coverage of frequency-based alternatives.
+
+Eight protected-Racket evaluations establish the finite counterexample. Search
+stopped after 30 default lesson windows; this is not a prevalence estimate.
+Retained exact source/program/input/output evidence and a replay script live in
+`counterexamples/review-8c91de8993832d58/`. Finding remains unresolved; no generator,
+rule or existing approval was changed. A bounded repair should teach conflict
+examples with color-frequency rankings inconsistent with quadrant priority, or
+reject lessons where this rival survives and changes the query.
